  "steps": [
    "Heat olive oil in a 12-inch skillet over medium heat for 1 minute until shimmering. Add the yellow onion and red bell pepper; cook for 5 to 6 minutes, stirring occasionally, until vegetables soft and onions become translucent.",
    "Stir in the minced garlic, ground cumin, smoked paprika, red pepper flakes, salt, and black pepper. Cook for 1 minute over medium heat, stirring constantly, until highly fragrant.",
    "Pour in crushed tomatoes and rinsed white cannellini beans. Bring sauce to a simmer over medium-high heat, then reduce heat to medium-low and simmer uncovered for 8 to 10 minutes, stirring occasionally, until sauce thickens slightly.",
    "Use a large spoon to make 8 small wells in the tomato-bean mixture. Carefully crack 1 egg into each well. Scatter crumbled feta cheese evenly across the top of sauce between the eggs.",
    "Cover skillet tightly with a lid and cook on medium-low heat for 5 to 7 minutes, until egg whites are fully set and opaque while yolks remain runny.",
    "Remove skillet from heat. Dollop plain Greek yogurt over the top, sprinkle with chopped fresh parsley, and serve immediately."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "To meal prep, prepare the tomato and white bean base ahead of time; store in the fridge for up to 4 days and reheat before poaching fresh eggs.",
    "Swap cannellini beans for chickpeas or dark red kidney beans if desired for a slightly different texture.",
    "Keep the skillet covered during the final cooking step so steam sets the egg whites evenly without overcooking the yolks."
  ],
  "storage": "Store leftover tomato-bean sauce in an airtight container in the fridge for up to 4 days. Poach eggs fresh when serving.",
